{"id":"d2e8cac4-b239-43f1-af6d-c625737362f3","name":"NYC 3D Model by Community District","type":"Public","description":"\n         <div id=\"internal-head\" class=\"internal-header\">\n            <div class=\"column\">\n               <div id=\"breadcrumb\"><a class=\"crumb em--md\" href=\"index_v2.html\">Home </a></div>\n               <div class=\"section-head\">NYC 3D Model by Community District</div>\n               <div class=\"section-head-description\"></div>\n            </div>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"content-container resource\">\n            <aside>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link\" href=\"#overview\">Overview</a>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link\" href=\"#recent-release\">Most Recent Release</a>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link sub-link\" href=\"#manhattan\">Manhattan</a>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link sub-link\" href=\"#bronx\">The Bronx</a>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link sub-link\" href=\"#brooklyn\">Brooklyn</a>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link sub-link\" href=\"#queens\">Queens</a>\n               <a class=\"arrow-link sub-link\" href=\"#staten_island\">Staten Island</a>\n\n               <a class=\"arrow-link\" href=\"#use-info\">Access & Use Information</a>\n            </aside>\n            <article>\n               <div class=\"main-section\" id=\"overview\">\n                  <p>\n                     The NYC 3D Model by Community District is a publicly available model consisting of every building in New York City present in\n                     2014. The model is based on DOITT&rsquo;s 2014 aerial survey, which provides roof structure details, including a high-level of\n                     detail for certain iconic buildings. The Department of City Planning imported and enhanced the DOITT files by converting the\n                     entire model into .3dm format, which is compatible with Rhinoceros 3D modeling software. DCP also divided the model into the\n                     City&rsquo;s 59 Community Districts and enriched each CD with base layers, including lots, streets, parks, and rail lines.\n                  </p>\n\n                  <p class=\"em--md\">\n                     Dataset: 3D Data<br />\n                     Update Frequency: As Needed\n                  </p>\n               </div>\n               <div class=\"main-section\" id=\"recent-release\">\n                  <h1>Most Recent Release</h1>\n                  <p class=\"copy--lg\">\n                     <span class=\"display--block copy--lg\">Latest Release: October 19, 2018</span>\n                     <span class=\"display--block copy--lg\">Date of Data: August 2018</span>\n                  </p>\n                  <div class=\"sub-section\" id=\"manhattan\">\n                     <h3>Manhattan</h3>\n                     <table class=\"orange\">\n                        <tr>\n                           <th>MN CD 01</th>\n                        </tr>\n                        <tr>\n                           <td>\n                              Battery Park City, Civic Center, Ellis Island, Governors Island, Liberty Island, South Street Seaport, Tribeca, Wall\n                              <div class=\"dataset-file-container\">\n                                 <a\n                                    class=\"card-btn download\"\n                                    href=\"https://s-media.nyc.gov/agencies/dcp/assets/files/zip/data-tools/bytes/nyc-3d-model/nyc_3dmodel_mn01.zip\"\n                                 >\n                                    Download File\n                                 </a>\n                              </div>\n                           </td>\n                        </tr>\n                        <tr>\n                           <th>MN CD 02</th>\n                        </tr>\n                        <tr>\n                           <td>\n                              Greenwich Village, Hudson Square, Little Italy, NoHo, SoHo, South Village, West V